From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peijin Zhang <peijin@ustc.edu>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:07:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Multiscale: reuse the scale-convolved residual and
 per-scale psf transforms

Per minor iteration, the residual convolved with the selected scale is taken
from the preceding peak search, which already computed it, and the
twice-convolved psfs and the transformed psf kernel of CorrectResidualDirty()
are made once per scale per major iteration. Each reuse is limited to 1 GiB.
Results are identical; 2048^2 multiscale deconvolution 4.18 -> 3.64 s.

